# ===========================================================================
# ALWAYS-TRACK ALLOWLIST  --  keep these rules LAST (last match wins).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: sync.ps1 was written 2026-07-08, silently untracked by the
# blanket `build_scripts/*` rule, then deleted from disk. Git never warned,
# because git cannot warn about a file it was never tracking. It was only
# recoverable because it happened to be committed once before the ignore rule
# landed. Every other tool in build_scripts/ had the same exposure.
#
# Tracking IS the safety net: delete a TRACKED file and `git status` shows a
# loud ` D`. Delete an IGNORED file and nothing happens at all.
#
# RULE: authored source (.py/.ps1/.java/.md) is tracked. Machine output stays
# ignored -- decompile dumps, logs, exports, caches. Never add a negation for
# *.txt, *.csv, *.log or any recompiler/decompiler output; those are large and
# game-derived.
#
# GOTCHA: git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a `!` under one
# never fires. Each level must be re-admitted first (`!dir/`), then its
# contents re-excluded (`dir/*`), then the wanted files negated.
# Verify any change with:  git check-ignore -v <path>   (no output = tracked)
# ===========================================================================

# Per-machine sync bookkeeping. Rewritten by sync.ps1 on both machines, so
# tracking it guarantees a conflict on every single sync.
_ClaudeMemory/

# build_scripts/* excluded above. Authored tools only; dumps/logs stay out.
!build_scripts/*.py
!build_scripts/*.ps1
# Stage B opcode conformance: the tools are tracked; out/ (test ELF, generated C++, results) is not.
!build_scripts/conformance/
build_scripts/conformance/*
!build_scripts/conformance/*.py
!build_scripts/conformance/*.ps1

# ghidra_scripts/ is swept up by `ghidra_*/`, so re-admit the dir explicitly.
!ghidra_scripts/
ghidra_scripts/*
!ghidra_scripts/*.py
!ghidra_scripts/*.java
!ghidra_scripts/*.md

# ida_scripts/ holds authored scripts AND large game-derived decompile dumps.
# Track the scripts; the dumps are *.txt and stay ignored.
!ida_scripts/
ida_scripts/*
!ida_scripts/idapy_ps2/
ida_scripts/idapy_ps2/*
!ida_scripts/idapy_ps2/*.py
!ida_scripts/idapy_ps2/*.md

# GS-dump replay harness inputs/outputs. The .gsr is a re-derivable export of a
# PCSX2 dump (build_scripts/gsdump_parse.py --emit-replay) and runs to megabytes.
gsdump/*
gsdump_replay*.bmp

